\f4\fs26 AgentState
\f1\fs24  and the 
\f4\fs26 context_schema
\f1\fs24  are 
\f0\b extensible
\f1\b0  \'97 you subclass/extend them to add whatever custom fields your app needs (mirrors how Claude/ChatGPT internally track your name, tier, preferences, etc., without it being literal chat history).\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 This is framework-agnostic in 
\f2\i concept
\f1\i0  \'97 Google's Agent Development Kit (ADK) has an equivalent "Agent Runtime"; other agent platforms use different names for the same underlying idea (deployment/runtime metadata, tool/context capabilities, etc.). The instructor pulled up ADK and a generic agent-CLI doc to show the same pattern under different names.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Framed as 
\f0\b "dependency injection" for tools and middleware
\f1\b0 : instead of hardcoding values or relying on global state, you inject runtime dependencies at agent-invocation time.\
